# ==========================================================================
# NOTE: this repository is intended to be published (GitHub Pages). A GitHub
# Pages SITE is always publicly reachable unless the organisation is on GitHub
# Enterprise Cloud — so treat everything that is not ignored here as world
# readable. Run `git status` before the first push and check the list yourself.
# ==========================================================================

# --- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------
# config.js is PUBLIC app configuration (branding, i18n, schema helpers) and is
# committed on purpose — the published site needs it. Secrets moved out of it
# into config.secrets.js; the .example template IS safe to commit.
config.secrets.js

# pipedrive.local.json holds the Pipedrive API token. The .example file next to
# it is the template and IS safe to commit — it contains no secret.
pipedrive.local.json

# Any other local override / credential file.
*.local.json
!pipedrive.local.example.json
.env
.env.*

# Sync bookkeeping and logs written by pipedrive-sync.mjs.
.sync/

# --- Customer data --------------------------------------------------------
# The board database (project cards, intake/proposal/report exports, product
# records) holds CUSTOMER data: company names, contacts, trial results and
# photos. It must never end up in the repository. The live database now lives in
# the SharePoint folder; what is left here is the pre-migration archive.
DataBasa Kanban/
DataBase Kanban/
DataBase Trial WorkFlow/
# Archived pre-SharePoint database + loose exports. Its contents happen to match
# the filename patterns below, but that is luck, not intent: anything dropped in
# there under another name would show up as untracked. Ignore the folder itself.
_OLD-*/
_ARCHIVE-*/

# Build output of publish.mjs: the public app tree, with its own git history and
# its own remote. Generated, so it must not be committed here as well.
_publish/
board.json
board.json.bak
products.json
projects/
products/

# Loose tool exports (these are customer data too, whatever they are called).
*_report_*.json
Intake Form_*.json
Validation Report*.json
perfotec_proposal_*.json
perfotec_report_*.json
_backups/

# --- OS / editor noise ----------------------------------------------------
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
~$*
node_modules/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Local test rigs ------------------------------------------------------
# board-fakefs.js binds an in-memory File System Access root so a tool can be
# driven without picking a real folder, and the *-test / *-old dashboard copies
# are that tool with its two script tags swapped to load it. They are whole
# copies of a file this repository already tracks, so git history already holds
# what they preserve. They also must not reach the published site: a committed
# dashboard-test.html would be a reachable page that looks like the dashboard
# but runs on a fake database.
*-fakefs.js
*-old.html
*-test.html
